sis\": \"The source approaches may preserve complementary predictive information, but redundancy or task interference may erase the smaller task-conditioning gain. Inherit the two committed source approaches, subject to implementation inspection in the next phase; test their combination against both frozen source bests, especially g0 at 0.8283262734957326. Cross representation replacement with task-conditioning removal, retain the available gradient-stop contrasts, and compare capacity and equal training exposure while measuring training/inference cost. Added utility predicts a repeat-confirmed macro-AUC improvement over both sources beyond capacity controls. Failure to exceed g0, equivalent gains from capacity alone, or disappearance under replacement controls opposes complementary utility; unchanged stop contrasts would leave gradient isolation unsupported. Report every task AUC/logloss trade-off. Reserve resources for attribution and repeat confirmation; freeze selection and comparison suite before one withheld assessment. No mechanism or novelty is established by the present summaries.\",\n    \"id\": \"g3-t001\",\n    \"status\": \"active\",\n    \"source_topic_ids\": [\n      \"g0-t000\",\n      \"g3-t000\"\n    ],\n    \"entry_trial_id\": \"g0-r0005-linear_moment\",\n    \"entry_auc\": 0.8283262734957326,\n    \"import_trial_refs\": [\n      \"g0-r0005-linear_moment\",\n      \"g3-r0004-click_score_stop\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
