{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"agent_message","text":"The code blocks click gradients only at the input to its private residual scorer; the shared moment and value paths still train. That stop was inherited from a weaker architecture, so its benefit here is unresolved.\n\nI’ll prepare a four-cell factorial: no stops, click-only stop, auxiliary-only stop, and both stops. This keeps parameter count and inference calculations fixed and tests whether the learning rule explains part of the gain. The proposal will also retain the observed click/cart regressions against the matched mean-routing control."}}
